Empty or thin cells. Science, mathematics and logic: none in 2024 (the Kant Yearbook 16 articles by Wilson, Sutherland, Wells and Alavi, and Seel on the Only Possible Argument, have CrossRef or S2 citation counts of 0 to 3; no 2024 monograph was found), and one entry each in 2022 and 2023. Aesthetics and teleology: no primary 2024 entry (Rueger's Element on pleasure and judgment, Williams in the Journal of Aesthetics and Art Criticism and Reiter and Geiger in the European Journal of Philosophy were screened out; Matherne and Russell carry the secondary tag). Edition and translation: no new Cambridge Edition volume or major new translation of a Kant text was found in any of the three years; Kant, Traume (2022, German, eds Kreimendahl and Oberhausen) and Walschots (2024, translations of Kant's contemporaries) are the only entries; the De Gruyter Kant Jubilee set of Klassiker Auslegen volumes (2024) consists of revised editions of existing commentaries and was not included; Immanuel Kant: Neue Reflexionen and Naturrecht Feyerabend (frommann-holzboog, 2024) were seen in CrossRef but not examined. Education, disability and animals: no entry in any of the three years (Muller, Kantianism for Animals, 2022, was screened out on a short abstract; the Oxford Handbook of Kant contains chapters on education, and on sex and gender, but no standalone work was found); gender is covered by Pascoe 2022, Rinne and Brecher 2023 and the Handbook chapter. Tercentenary material: the 14th International Kant Congress (Bonn, 2024) and the Kant 300 conferences were found only through web pages and journal reports; no proceedings volume dated 2024 was found, and anniversary special issues in English-language core venues were not found. Kant and AI or technology: Kim and Schonecker (2022), Aigner (2024, Low) and the screened-out Aylsworth and Castro, Kantian Ethics and the Attention Economy (Springer, 2024) are the only items; Kantian Review 2024 carries a review of the 2022 AI volume.
INCOMPLETE ENTRIES: baiasu2023kantianmind (book; summary grounded in a publisher page retrieved in-session; the NDPR review attached by the enrichment script was a review of an unrelated book, The Life of the Mind, and was removed). Other tool-handling notes: the enrichment script also attached a wrong NDPR review to timmons2022virtue (a review of a Heidegger lecture-course translation); it was removed and the S2 abstract was added from the in-session get_abstract output. Four journal entries whose DOIs are carried in the url field (pendlebury2022mind, stang2023schematism, fahmy2023merely, kinzel2024neokantian) were marked INCOMPLETE by the script because it looks up abstracts by the doi field; their abstracts were added from the in-session get_abstract outputs. S2 title-matched citation counts are missing or wrong for several books; CrossRef is-referenced-by-count is reported alongside. Source issues: S2 returned not-found errors for queries with a citation floor and rate-limit errors during enrichment; CORE returned an API error 500 during enrichment; the NDPR search is fuzzy, so every NDPR attachment was checked by title and author.

